{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise","id":1558048,"title":"V20 table for when Vampires fall into daysleep and when they rise?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-31T14:51:56-08:00","id":1558048,"title":"V20 table for when Vampires fall into daysleep and when they rise?","content":"I remember seeing a table somewhere, in a V20 book I think, which showed when you have to sleep / can wake, based on your Humanity/Path. The only detail I remember is that with a Humanity/Path of 10, you can wake at the moment of sunset, and fall asleep at the moment of sunrise, without any issues. I've searched the V20 corebook quite carefully but I can't find it anywhere!<br /> <br /> The Early Riser merit refers to the idea but no real details are given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T09:43:40-08:00","id":1558076,"title":"","content":"Is \u2018Daysleep\u2019 the same thing as torpor? (I\u2019ve generally understood the condition to be much the same, with duration being the key difference).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-02T17:11:29-08:00","id":1558086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558076#post1558076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is \u2018Daysleep\u2019 the same thing as torpor? (I\u2019ve generally understood the condition to be much the same, with duration being the key difference).</div> </div> </div> </div>To my memory, no.<br /> You can wake up from daysleep if disturbed. With torpor you have to wait out the minimum torpor duration based on your Road rating.<br /> Maybe there are rules on waking up from torpor for a few turns if disturbed though, and I have just forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T09:03:27-08:00","id":1558139,"title":"","content":"I swear to God I saw a chart in a VtM revised series - there have been threads like this before. This chart of when a vampire rises based on humanity seems like some of fever dream hallucination until someone combs through every book and definitively proves it exists or doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T11:10:49-08:00","id":1558146,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's the Mandela Effect. We all can remember this damn table, but no one can say where it is. \ud83d\ude06","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T12:04:19-08:00","id":1558147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558146#post1558146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's the Mandela Effect. We all can remember this damn table, but no one can say where it is. \ud83d\ude06</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, like Berenstein Bears vs Berenstain Bears. I do have a feeling that I did look at a chart on a house rule collator like BJ Zanzibar's website back in the day. But I swear to God I read something in a VtM book 20 years ago, but can't remember which one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-06T23:37:48-08:00","id":1558157,"title":"","content":"I think I saw it in VDA20. I'm quite sure of it. There should be a table for how long one stays in torpor based on Road score and a paragraph on when one wakes up based on Road score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-07T11:09:28-08:00","id":1558163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558157#post1558157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I saw it in VDA20. I'm quite sure of it. There should be a table for how long one stays in torpor based on Road score and a paragraph on when one wakes up based on Road score.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked up my VtDA pdf and yes, page 351 has a chart for road score and torpor length, and says &quot;Following this rest, the player may spend a blood point and make a roll to awaken (see p. 360) to rise.&quot; Page 360 has no awakening rules at all or chart on when you wake up based on road score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T04:09:02-08:00","id":1558179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558163#post1558163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I looked up my VtDA pdf and yes, page 351 has a chart for road score and torpor length, and says &quot;Following this rest, the player may spend a blood point and make a roll to awaken (see p. 360) to rise.&quot; Page 360 has no awakening rules at all or chart on when you wake up based on road score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there's the torpor length chart, but I distinctly remember a book, can't remember which one, having a chart that tells you when you wake each night, and when you sleep, relative to sunrise/sunset and your Humanity! Maybe it was homebrew in a server I was in? I remember it being in a PDF though, tbh!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T04:30:56-08:00","id":1558180,"title":"","content":"I just ignore it anyway. It's just more dramatic for the ancient vampire lord to awaken explosively the moment the sun falls below the horizon. The idea that a hunter has an extra hour after sunset to break into his coffin-room because the vampire is especially evil is just....sigh...to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T05:34:39-08:00","id":1558184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558180#post1558180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just ignore it anyway. It's just more dramatic for the ancient vampire lord to awaken explosively the moment the sun falls below the horizon. The idea that a hunter has an extra hour after sunset to break into his coffin-room because the vampire is especially evil is just....sigh...to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or not evil enough, depending on his path...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-08T11:51:02-08:00","id":1558187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558048-v20-table-for-when-vampires-fall-into-daysleep-and-when-they-rise?p=1558163#post1558163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I looked up my VtDA pdf and yes, page 351 has a chart for road score and torpor length, and says &quot;Following this rest, the player may spend a blood point and make a roll to awaken (see p. 360) to rise.&quot; Page 360 has no awakening rules at all or chart on when you wake up based on road score.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nightly wake up time may be in the introduction to how Road works. As for p.360 not having that, the book has some problems, but there are some rules on rolls to wake up in the chapter on sample or common rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T06:10:09-07:00","id":1558730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Characters with higher Road ratings have come to terms with themselves, and thus have less inner turmoil. As result, they rise earlier in the evening. There are no hard numbers on this, but a character with seven or more dots in her Road will rise just before the sun sets, and a character with four or fewer will rise up to an hour after. </div> </div> </div>Found what DAV20 has to say on it! But no table to be seen. I know there was one SOMEWHERE, but this paragraph definitely suffices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}